bucharest-lite (1.10.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 1.10.0: Linux audio, three-point editing, masks, GPU compositor
    - ALSA output backend (dlopen, BL_AUDIO_DEVICE, null-sink fallback) and a
      fixed WinMM sink that interleaves planar frames
    - Persistent preview audio readers with resampling, channel mapping,
      gain/pan/mute/solo, speed and reverse playback
    - Source Monitor dock with in/out marks and insert/overwrite three-point
      edits (',' '.' Alt+I Alt+O), linked A/V in one undo step
    - Polygon rotoscoping masks with Catmull-Rom smoothing, feather, opacity,
      invert and an Inspector Masks editor; serialised and applied in preview
      and export
    - Pluggable compositor with an optional OpenGL 3.3 backend
      (BL_COMPOSITOR=gpu|auto) and CPU fallback; CPU remains the default

 -- L Hustla <harlemi@example.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200

bucharest-lite (1.9.15-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 1.9.15: proxy editing infrastructure — auto-generate low-res proxies for smooth 4K+ editing
    - Global "Use Proxies" toolbar button
    - Proxy status badges on timeline clips (✓/⟳/✕ indicators)
    - Per-clip proxy override persistence in project JSON
    - Proxy preferences dialog (directory, threshold, CRF, codec, concurrency)
    - Proxy cleanup when media removed from bin
    - Proxy generation progress in status bar
    - Undo/redo history panel (View → Undo History…, Ctrl+7)
    - Regression fixes: timeline lane heights, EditMode restore clamp, codec-aware proxy FFmpeg args, shell-free runProcess

 -- L Hustla <harlemi@example.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:45:00 +0300
